# tally 2.2.1 P43 S1 (L §4.4 l.669, §6.1 l.1797): the day of movements stated same, one comparison of the days each side
# can take: a day pinned to a window against a day: the balance books it once (review g2fix same/s1_dayonly);
# two days that differ stay HOLE-SAME after both (P43, n2); unpinned, after the window too, the window's hole (P45 d).
=== s1_dayonly.tally
model s1
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1: money PLN
input d1: date
input d2: date
move in1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
move in2: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  d2 = 2026-03-09 "s"
  same in1 = in2
ask b4: bal(konto, 2026-03-04)
ask b7: bal(konto, 2026-03-07)
ask b31: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
ask f: flows(konto, 2026-03)
ask s0: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask dy: m.day for m in transfers over 2026-03
ask pw: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) with d2 = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
ask pq: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) with d2 = 2026-03-05
=== expect b4 b31 pw pq dy
b4: 500.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
b31: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but leg cash differs on 2026-03-05, 2026-03-09: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 100.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  cut 2026-01-01
pw: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a balance" (in2)
  pinned: d2 = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
  unknown day: d2
  cut 2026-01-01
pq: 600.00 PLN
  pinned: d2 = 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-01-01
dy (m = in1): ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the day of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 2026-03-05 (in1) and 2026-03-09 (in2)" (in1, in2)
  cut 2026-01-01
